  "steps": [
    "Agrodulce: pulse the peppers, vinegar, and garlic in a food processor to a medium-coarse texture.",
    "In a medium pot over medium heat, combine the honey and pepper mixture. Bring to a boil and cook, stirring often and watching for boil-overs, until reduced by half. Taste and adjust with more vinegar and salt.",
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F. Put the chicken skin side up in a baking dish, season both sides with the salt and pepper, and drizzle with the oil. Bake until the skin starts to turn golden, 10 to 15 minutes.",
    "Spoon agrodulce over the chicken and bake until the sauce is sticky and the thickest thigh reads 165°F, about 5 minutes more.",
    "Rest the chicken 5 minutes, then cut each thigh in half.",
    "Ranch: whisk the mayonnaise, sour cream, mustard, lemon zest and juice, parsley, dill, chives, and grated garlic. Season with salt and pepper.",
    "Slaw: toss the jalapeños, yellow peppers, pickles, dill, parsley, chives, and onion with the olive oil and lemon juice. Season with salt and pepper.",
    "Build each slider: ranch on the roll, a piece of chicken, a spoonful of extra agrodulce, then slaw."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "If the thighs have not reached 165°F after the glaze goes on, keep baking a few minutes more before resting them.",
    "Wear gloves when handling the scotch bonnet, and seed it for less heat.",
    "The agrodulce makes far more than 6 thighs need; refrigerate the rest in a jar for other uses.",
    "In the video, Matty finishes the sliders with toasted sesame seeds and extra pickled peppers."
  ],
